  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-11T13:01:40.759Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Using my own world for example, there is a mismatch of words used on the website vs in the worlds menu. As shown on the website, my world was first created as a private world on `Sept 15 2019` before I decided to make it fully public (published) on `Dec 21 2019`. Now a private world technically isn't published, so could change the wording in the world menu to \"Created\" instead, keeping the original creation date, or keep as Published but swap the date over to the actual \"Published\" date. I'm personally for the former.",
